; Meadow — NEW TerrainDefinition (habitat-tiers ruling, 2026-09-04 -> task-8-brief.md).
; VALUES BELOW ARE A PROPOSAL AWAITING HUMAN SIGN-OFF (same posture as every other
; terrain's cost/scale/model choices in this codebase; see barn.tres for the same
; convention on the buildings side).
;
; WHY IT EXISTS: rich grazing terrain, and the first real SOURCE for the long-dormant
; `flowers` habitat tag (AnimalDefinition.HABITAT_TAGS has carried `flowers` with no
; emitter since it was added — this closes that gap). Paired with Scrub as the second half
; of the new grazing-terrain split: Meadow is the `open_grass`-family pick (same emission
; as plain Grass, plus `flowers`), Scrub is the `browse`-family pick.
;
; emitted_tags = ["open_grass", "flowers"] is DECIDED by the habitat-tiers ruling
; (task-8-brief.md's table). No radius, no weight, no threshold — the v1 tag model
; (-> D-25) applies unchanged.
;
; cost = 0 — natural terrain, "nature is free" (terrain.md's one pricing rule, unchanged by
; this task).
;
; MODEL_SCENE: Meadow.tscn (CC0, Stylized Nature MegaKit) — see that scene's own header for
; full sourcing/scale detail. Single variant; a multi-variant look-pass is out of scope
; here, same posture Grass/Rock/Wild grass all started with before their own later passes.
;
; PLAYER-VISIBLE CONSEQUENCE: Meadow is a new, free-to-paint entry in the Terraform
; palette — flagged prominently per this task's brief, not buried in a count bump.
;
; No `fact_text` copy yet — Content Pipeline step 5 (Content Writer), explicitly out of
; scope for this task.
; GRASS-FAMILY REWORK (2026-09-08), model_scenes 1 -> 3, applying the Grass calibration
; baseline the human signed off the same day. Variants: Meadow (flower clumps — the shipped
; look, now over a real grass base), MeadowScattered (single blooms spread thin) and
; MeadowMixed (both, densest). All 3 equal weight in pick_variant(); a painted meadow now
; alternates per tile via D-42's stable hash instead of stamping one identical tile.
;
; THE BIG VISUAL CHANGE IS THE GRASS BASE. Meadow previously carried flowers on a bare tinted
; slab, so next to Grass's dense lawn it read as "slab with props" despite both terrains
; emitting `open_grass`. All 3 variants now use the same blade mesh, scale and MultiMesh
; treatment Grass does, leaving the FLOWERS as the only difference between the two terrains —
; which is exactly the tag difference, and is the prop-vocabulary partition working as
; intended (see GrassClover.tscn's header).
;
; NO PICKER CONSEQUENCE: `meadow` is not a style-picker category and has no style ids at all
; (WorldRoot._model_scenes_for_category handles only house/forest/wild_grass), so this is pure
; per-tile variety. Contrast wild_grass.tres, which is why that terrain was held at 1 variant.
;
; 2 NEW IMPORTS, MegaKit, CC0 1.0, audit gate re-checked: Flower_3_Single, Flower_4_Single.
; New scales (0.14505 / 0.12401, both to the established ~0.30 tile-unit flower target) are
; FIRST-PASS PROPOSALS; the carried-over Group scales are unchanged.
